governor-bounty-desc-omnizine = The Confederate Command demands Omnizine. Our supplies are empty, and doctors have started treating people with placebos and prayers. Deliver 100 units before we lose our last medics.

governor-bounty-desc-oligomers = The science department blew something up again and is now begging for Polypyrylium Oligomers. They say it will save their experiment. We think they just want to see something catch fire in a new color.

governor-bounty-desc-ambuzol-plus = Ambuzol+ needed urgently! Our fighters "ACCIDENTALLY" mixed up romerol tablets with tricadrazine again. 150 units — and we might stop this epidemic.

governor-bounty-desc-necrosol = Command is ordering Necrosol. Medics claim it can bring back to life even that guy who "slightly" fried himself in the engine yesterday. Deliver 150 units before our doctors start conducting necromancy sessions without a license.

governor-bounty-desc-vestine = Vestine is a very rare precursor for creating cool drugs. Our pharmacists are tired of brewing potions from plantain and birch buds, they need this component. Deliver 30 units before they start performing rituals over reactors with prayers to the gods of chemistry.

governor-bounty-desc-aphrodisiac = Command has gone crazy again. They urgently need an aphrodisiac for some reason. Someone clearly wants to throw a "corporate party" in the officer's mess. We don't ask, we just obey.

governor-bounty-desc-brownies = The station's head chef demands special brownies. Says the crew is too stressed. We suspect he just wants to get high after his shift. Deliver the batch.

governor-bounty-desc-bearsteak = Frontier hunters complain there's no normal food on the station. We ordered bearsteak fillet so they'd stop stealing canned goods from the armory. Deliver at least one steak before they start hunting crew members.

governor-bounty-desc-carp-sushi = Command decided to throw a gala dinner for important guests. They demand space carp nigiri! Because regular fish is for plebeians. Deliver it before our cooks quit to hell and back.

governor-bounty-desc-anomaly-steak = Bored? Command demands anomaly steak. They say after eating it, chakras open, saucers fly, and wishes come true. Actually, the boss just wants to feel like a superhero. Deliver this weird meat.

governor-bounty-desc-poutine = Our miners are on strike! Actually, they're just sitting around whining that they're sick of dry rations. They want poutine — fries with cheese and gravy. Deliver it before they start demanding caviar buffets.

governor-bounty-desc-sashimi = The officer corps thinks they're gourmets. They urgently need sashimi because "sushi is so vulgar." Deliver it before they start ordering black caviar by the truckload.

governor-bounty-desc-dragon-omelette = Command got inspired by fantasy and wants dragon omelette. Apparently they watched too many cartoons as kids. Deliver it so they stop calling each other "Lords of the Rings" and start working.

governor-bounty-desc-trophy = The Confederate Command collects trophies. They don't care whose trophy it is — beast, enemy, or a randomly flying asteroid. Bring any so they can finally hang something on the bare wall instead of cat posters.

governor-bounty-desc-ore-plasma = Urgent! Plasma ore. Our reactors are running on pure faith and technicians' prayers. 100 units — and we won't drift in the dark like mindless rocks.

governor-bounty-desc-ore-uranium = Uranium needed for reactors and, uh, "peaceful" research. We're not building a bomb, honest. The admiral just wants his office to glow in the dark. Green.

governor-bounty-desc-ore-silver = Silver! Our circuits burn more often than rookies' toast. Technicians beg for 100 units, or they'll start soldering wires with their own fingers. And we already have a personnel shortage.

governor-bounty-desc-ore-gold = Gold! The admiral wants to melt it into a statue of his beloved self. But officially — for electronics. Deliver 100 units before he starts casting medals for his favorite officers (spoiler: he'll only give them to himself).

governor-bounty-desc-steel-ore = We've run out of iron ore. The station is falling apart, we're patching holes with duct tape and hope. Deliver 100 units before we start dismantling the admiral's cabin for spare parts. (Joke. Or not.)

governor-bounty-desc-bananium = Someone decided bananium is a great idea. Why do we need this stupid banana alloy? Command wants to make a "funny" mine for enemies. Or a new slot machine. We don't even know what to expect from them anymore. Deliver 10 units before they start going bananas themselves.

governor-bounty-desc-diamond = Diamonds! The tech department is crying and praying over laser installations that overheat every single day. They need diamonds for cooling. Or diamond armor. Or just to sparkle. Deliver 10 units.

governor-bounty-desc-bluespace = Bluespace ore! Cartographers lost the entire sector again and want to build a new teleporter to find their way home. Deliver 5 units before they fly into a parallel universe for cigarettes.

governor-bounty-desc-scaf = SCAF suit. No, this is not a joke. One of our officers managed to tear his suit open while opening a can of food. Now he needs a new one. Deliver it before he wraps himself in a trash bag and goes into open space to breathe "fresh air."
